      "id": 1,
      "text": "Manhattan Beach got its name in 1902 from developer Stewart Merrill, who named it after his New York home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Manhattan Beach Historical Society museum sits in Polliwog Park, preserving the city’s artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s first railroad tracks appeared in 1888, built by Santa Fe Railroad, later called Shore Acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Manhattan Beach was a filming hotspot: movies like Against All Odds (1983) and music videos such as Macklemore’s “White Walls” were shot along The Strand.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lifeguard stations line the entire beach, and crews clean and groom it daily, keeping the sands pristine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Beach%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Manhattan Beach Library began as a subscription library in 1910, founded by the Neptunian Women’s Club.",
